00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:33,880
psychology and economics. Now there's a more advanced formula called Bayes' Rule, which

36
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:39,720
is the one that economists talk about a lot more. So, Bayes' Rule links the probability

37
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:44,720
of A given B to the probability of B given A. So Bayes' Rule states the probability of

38
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:52,440
A given B is equal to the probability of B given A times the probability of A all over

39
00:03:52,440 --> 00:04:01,840
the probability of B given A times the probability of A plus the probability of B given not A

40
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:07,760
, tilde means not, times the probability of not A. And that is Bayes' Rule, which I'm

41
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:11,120
I'm sure everyone just immediately looks at it and sees that's got to be true, of course.

